 "hook": {
  "text": "A UNICORN...\n4,000 YEARS AGO?",
  "until": 3.4,
  "y": 0.12,
  "size": 110,
  "accent": [
   "UNICORN..."
  ]
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "This seal is four thousand years old. Look at the animal.",
   "emph": [
    "animal."
   ],
   "caption": "This seal is 4,000 years old. Look at the animal."
  },
  {
   "text": "One horn. A unicorn.",
   "emph": [
    "unicorn."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And it's on nearly seven of every ten seals.",
   "emph": [
    "7",
    "10"
   ],
   "caption": "And it's on nearly 7 of every 10 seals."
  },
  {
   "text": "Even the seal from Iraq in Part Two... is a unicorn.",
   "emph": [
    "iraq",
    "unicorn."
   ],
   "caption": "Even the seal from Iraq in Part 2... is a unicorn."
  },
  {
   "text": "The elephants and tigers they carved really roamed the Indus. So was the unicorn real too... or pure myth?",
   "emph": [
    "real",
    "myth?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Some say it's just a bull, one horn hiding the other.",
   "emph": [
    "bull,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Others point to clay figures with just one horn.",
   "emph": [
    "one",
    "horn."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And always in front of it, a strange object. Incense burner? Sacred filter? No one knows.",
   "emph": [
    "strange"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, around nineteen hundred BC, the unicorn vanished... along with their writing.",
   "emph": [
    "vanished..."
   ],
   "caption": "Then, around 1900 BC, the unicorn vanished... along with their writing."
  },
  {
   "text": "Fifteen hundred years later, a Greek doctor wrote of a one-horned beast in India.",
   "emph": [
    "one-horned"
   ],
   "caption": "1,500 years later, a Greek doctor wrote of a one-horned beast in India."
  },
  {
   "text": "Most experts think he meant a rhino. Or was it a faint memory of the Indus unicorn?",
   "emph": [
    "rhino.",
    "memory"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And on one rare seal, the animals gather around a figure... sitting like a yogi.",
   "emph": [
    "yogi."
   ]
  }
 ],
